WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.540
Present Day

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.490
Present Time

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.240
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:28.440
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:33.190
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:38.460
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.860
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.330
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:49.090
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:54.750
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.870
I have lost it all

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:26.890
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.530
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:34.740
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.280
I am losing

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:41.480
Help me to breathe

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.620
Oh, okay. So that's how it works.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:09.170
I had no idea the world was this simple.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:14.170
I always thought the world was such a big and scary place,

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.680
but once you figure it out, it's all so easy.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.150
See? I told you it would be.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.650
That's terrible, Lain!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.420
I can't believe you just said that!

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.440
Lain...

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.580
I know, but it's true!

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.620
That's the first I've heard of it!

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.790
What does it mean?

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.690
Acting all high and mighty again, huh, Lain?

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.890
That reminds me, Juri.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.460
What?

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:27.720
You should just rewrite bad memories.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.330
But that's...

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.670
But that's...

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.330
Unbelievable...

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.170
Aw, come on!

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.840
People only have substance within the memories of others.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.500
That's why there were all kinds of me's.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.300
There weren't a lot of me's,

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.140
I was just inside all sorts of people, that's all.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.660
Really, no kidding?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.890
Come on, Taro, who are you talking to?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.500
W-What's up?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.090
You know, I...

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.710
I kissed an angel.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.220
Taro...

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:57.140
Lain...

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.510
Protocol Seven is expected to allow the seamless sharing of information

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:12.920
between the Wired and the real world.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:16.560
And now, the following message...

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:22.500
Let's all love Lain!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.500
All the functions of the human body, without exception,

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.250
can be put into words and described in materialistic terms.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.290
The body is nothing but a machine.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:45.430
If the physical limitations of the body restrict mankind's evolution,

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.120
it would be as if the fall of the species called "man"

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.920
had already been decided by a God that doesn't even exist.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.100
The information etched inside humans isn't only that which

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.760
they themselves have acquired as individuals.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.770
This species called man is connected to his predecessors,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.900
and information has accumulated within him.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.820
If that information isn't shared, it's meaningless. Mere data.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.610
Mankind can evolve. Evolve by their own power.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.860
But to do that, they must first know what they truly are.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.690
What do you think you are?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.460
Originally, people were connected to each other.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.220
All I've done is to make things as they once were.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.800
That's what you have done, Lain.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.910
So you can do anything you want.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.530
I thought you quit smoking.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:36.060
Why is this happening? We did exactly what we were told to do!

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.500
It means that our client wasn't the only one who thought that

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.410
those computer geeks playing "secret society" would be trouble.

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:45.940
What do you mean?

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.090
Our client was in contact with Masami Eiri.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.300
No, maybe Eiri was behind it all.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:59.450
Enough about Eiri, okay?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.150
The guy's dead.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.630
He's not dead.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.140
Whether he had a body or not never mattered.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.580
It never mattered.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.210
Are you serious?

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:05.390
Payment for services rendered, huh?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.080
You've been using us, haven't you?!

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.420
Interpret it any way you like.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.420
You want us to leave town, huh? And go where?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:23.180
I suppose a place with no power lines that isn't covered by a satellite.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:27.410
There's no place like that on Earth, and you know it!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:32.360
If you're going to run, you'll have to find a place like that.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.420
What's going to happen?

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.900
What are you planning to do

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:45.330
by connecting the Wired to the real world without any devices?

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.250
Something wonderful is going to happen.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:56.260
I'm looking forward to it. Aren't you?

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.820
What the...?

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.330
What's wrong?!

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.370
What are you seeing?!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.870
Hey!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.470
Iwakura

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:25.950
Lain?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.130
No!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.920
This is Lain's room?

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.250
Lain?

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:19.770
L-Lain!

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.900
A... risu?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.310
What did you do?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.420
Nothing.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.160
I've just been watching.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.520
Watching what?

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:47.720
I... I thought I had gone crazy.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.430
But I didn't!

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.430
Lain! Why did you leave only me?

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:59.100
Why did you only leave my memories alone?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:06.110
Why do I always have to remember all those horrible things?!

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:10.110
Do you hate me that much, Lain?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:16.160
I... I can't take this!

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.800
No... You've got it all wrong, Arisu.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:24.370
I didn't want to hurt you.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:27.300
Liar! Look at what you've done!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.710
But you're okay, aren't you, Arisu?

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:38.720
You were my friend, even without connecting with me, Arisu.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.560
What are you saying?

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.090
You're my only friend, Arisu.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.290
Even without connecting with me.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.030
"Connecting"? W-What do you mean?

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.300
Connecting to me... And everyone...

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.770
S-Stop!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.920
I love you, Arisu.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.090
Do you know what you're saying, Lain?

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:12.250
Humans were originally connected at an unconscious level.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.710
I reconnected them, that's all.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.180
Lain, you?

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.640
I don't do anything.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.470
It doesn't matter which is real, this side or the other.

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:26.930
I was in both.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:31.070
I'm a program designed to destroy the barrier

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:33.170
between the Wired and the real world.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.200
You're a program, Lain?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:41.380
You and everyone else, Arisu, you're just applications.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.770
The truth is, you don't need bodies.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.840
You're wrong.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:19.480
I don't really understand what you're saying, but I think you're wrong.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:26.040
Your body's cold, but you're alive, Lain.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:30.040
Mine, too. See?

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.770
See? My heart...

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.770
...it's beating.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.510
Beating... Beating...

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.780
But why? Why's it beating like that?

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:58.280
Because I'm scared. It's pounding because I'm scared.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.360
But you're smiling, Arisu.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:04.960
Yeah, I guess I am. But I'm scared.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.710
I've always been scared. I wonder why?

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.200
I wonder why?

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:13.090
Because she's afraid of losing her body.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.940
All sensations are caused by impulses in the brain.

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:20.370
You just need to block the unpleasant impulses.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:24.720
Select only the happy, pleasant ones.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.840
Really?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.600
Lain? Who are you talking to?

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:35.650
If you really love her, why don't you connect with her?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.320
I'm not sure.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.400
Lain? Who are you talking to?

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:42.490
Lain!

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:44.970
You must have a bug.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:50.080
Very well. I'll take my time and give you a thorough debugging.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.280
Come, Lain.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:07.020
What I don't understand is you, God.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:11.020
Y-You're... talking to God?

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:15.520
What don't you understand, Lain?

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:21.100
What you did was to remove devices from the Wired.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:25.480
Phones, television, the network...

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.080
Without those, you couldn't have done anything.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:33.580
Yes. Those are things which accompanied human evolution.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:37.790
Humans who are further evolved than others

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.260
have a right to greater abilities.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:46.560
Who gave you those rights?

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:54.070
The program that inserted code synched to the Earth's

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:56.280
characteristic frequency into the Protocol Seven code,

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.900
which would raise the collective unconscious to the conscious level.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:04.410
Did you really come up with the idea by yourself?

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.450
What are you getting at?

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:11.150
No, it can't be... It can't be!

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:13.720
Are you telling me that there really is a God?!

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:24.380
It doesn't matter. With no body, you can't understand.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:28.800
It's a lie! I... I'm omnipotent!

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:32.940
I gave you a body here in the real world!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.350
You were omnipresent, scattered through the Wired! I gave you an ego!

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.510
You mean to say...

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.180
If that's true of me, what about you?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.780
I'm different! I...

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:02.240
The Wired isn't an upper layer of the real world.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.800
What do you mean?

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.760
Inside the Wired, you were God, all right.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.450
But what about before the Wired was created?

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:15.270
You're just an acting God, standing in for someone

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:18.950
who was waiting for the Wired to reach its current state.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.090
An "acting" God?!

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.920
That can't be!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.260
Arisu!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:37.620
A body doesn't mean anything to you, right?

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.180
No!

00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:32.480
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:32.480
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:36.390
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:36.390
now I am punished.

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:42.690
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:42.690
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:49.600
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:49.600
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:56.150 --> 00:23:00.790
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:56.150 --> 00:23:00.790
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:05.240
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:05.240
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:11.430
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:11.430
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:18.670
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:18.670
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:26.720
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:26.720
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:36.630
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:36.630
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:42.240
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:42.240
You probably don't know

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:49.950
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:49.950
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
